 "notes": "ADMX haloscope. Main result Fig.4 (run1c_sensitivity.png), 90% C.L. upper limit on g_agamma vs axion mass over 3.3-4.2 mueV (~800-1015 MHz). Figure is a raster PNG with no ancillary data file; boundary recovered by red-pixel color extraction (bright red = Maxwellian). Two curves shown: Maxwellian (boosted Maxwell-Boltzmann, rho=0.45 GeV/cc) and N-body (rho=0.6 GeV/cc, slightly more stringent/deeper). Reported the Maxwellian curve as the paper-native main result (standard halo, listed first); N-body reaches ~10-20% lower g. Per-density values reported without rescaling per task card. x-axis calibrated from top mass ticks (2.6-4.2 mueV); y-axis (log) calibrated using the plotted KSVZ and DFSZ dashed reference lines with analytic g_KSVZ=alpha/(2pi f_a)*1.92, f_a=5.7e12/m_a[mueV] GeV, giving decade=1968 px (validated to <1%% at two masses). Excluded-region lower boundary is jagged (scan-to-scan sensitivity); points are the median per-mass-bin boundary of the bright-red region (~80 bins) after masking the red \"ADMX (this work)\" text label and the legend swatches. Limit sits between DFSZ (~5e-16) and KSVZ (~1.3-1.5e-15), consistent with paper claim of ruling out KSVZ over 3.3-4.2 and DFSZ over 3.9-4.1 mueV.",
